WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.880
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.560
 You're out there fighting
with Angelina Jolie.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:12.240
It's like, what
else do you need?

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:16.890
 Why not?

00:00:16.890 --> 00:00:26.020
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.240
 The Eternals are a
group of Super Heroes

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:31.090
who have been around for
at least 7,000 years.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.760
 Created by the Celestials,
sent to Earth to protect

00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:35.620
humankind from the Deviants.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.530
 Fighting to prevent
the end of the world,

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:41.480
or the end of human
civilization as we know it,

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.960
so I don't think the stakes
get much higher than that.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:50.270
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:50.270 --> 00:00:55.010
 For me, to be an Eternal
has many different meanings.

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:58.340
As the character, It
gives me a sense of duty,

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:00.170
because I am in
charge of the mission.

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:05.930
And personally, it gives me
a sense of hope for change.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:11.720
I am Latina, and also
Arab, and also in my 50s.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:14.930
It would have been almost
unimaginable that I

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.750
would become a superhero now.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:19.970
 I feel like what
it means to be

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:22.790
an Eternal is
becoming a reflection

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:25.500
of people who have been here.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:27.230
And I think that
the Eternals let

00:01:27.230 --> 00:01:31.901
people have an insight into how
wonderful humankind has been.

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:37.090
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:37.090 --> 00:01:38.890
 If I could, I
would only work with

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:40.240
Chloé Zhao from here on out.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.830
If Chloé called me
and was like hey,

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.680
I'm just going to put
you in everything I do,

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.930
I would be like, great.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.400
 It's an incredible
group that came

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.600
together to make this film.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:53.210
We all come from very different
backgrounds and cultures,

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.300
and it's an amazing
mix of people.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.160
 Once we finally came
together, and we're

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.270
all in our super suits
and got to see each other,

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:02.030
it was the most
amazing experience.

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:04.060
I think I cried.

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.540
I think I cried, and it still
is one of the most memorable

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.160
moments I've ever had.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.479
 It's like a big family.

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:12.070
Everyone was lovely.

00:02:12.070 --> 00:02:15.980
A big movie of that scale is a
bit intimidating to go on to.

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:17.470
 Chloé was our captain.

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:22.660
She listened and took my
ideas on building the action.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:23.920
Great teamwork.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:25.600
Great communication.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:27.053
I was very happy.

00:02:27.053 --> 00:02:32.980
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:37.690
 She shows her primary super
strength to be a speedster,

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.570
but also very intelligent.

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:42.340
I think that combination
of both of those

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.600
makes Makkari very powerful.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.720
 How am I alike or
different from Ikaris?

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:47.860
Well, very different.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.170
I can't fly, I can't shoot
lasers out of my eyes,

00:02:50.170 --> 00:02:51.910
I don't have super
strength, all of the things

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:53.740
I would very much like to have.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:56.350
 My character,
although she's an alien

00:02:56.350 --> 00:02:58.480
and doesn't have any children,
has a very strong sense

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:00.850
of motherhood for the
rest of the Eternals,

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.400
and I have always had that.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.320
She likes to boss
people around, and I

00:03:05.320 --> 00:03:07.120
have always had that, too.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.270
 She's a free spirit.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.730
She's very loyal.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:14.025
I would say I have quite a lot
of overlap with her, actually.

00:03:14.025 --> 00:03:19.370
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.410
 One of my favorite
moments to shoot, I suppose,

00:03:21.410 --> 00:03:27.110
was filming in Camden in London,
where I was on a crane on wires

00:03:27.110 --> 00:03:30.950
and I'm flying and
landing on the street.

00:03:30.950 --> 00:03:34.370
It was really fun, just because
I'm above the bridge in Camden,

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:37.220
and you get to see this kind
of bird's eye view of streets

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:38.510
that I've walked for many years.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.220
So I got to see it
from a different angle.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:43.940
 I am excited to see the
spectacle and the big action

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:46.790
pieces, and also
the more intimate

00:03:46.790 --> 00:03:49.560
character driven beats as well.

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:51.920
 This is an
incredibly epic movie.

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.320
I mean, the scale of
it, the story of it,

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.780
it's unlike anything I think
Marvel has ever done before.

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.760
As far as ensembles go,
this is one of the best

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:00.170
ensembles I've ever been with.

00:04:00.170 --> 00:04:02.960
You know, it was an incredibly
emotional ride, which I think

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:04.700
the viewer will experience
when they watch it,

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:07.780
because it's thousands
of years in the making.

